LIMITS
Fast startup captures old handle inventories, not every old descriptor.
First later descriptor of an unknown baseline handle only seeds identity;
reuse before that first observation cannot be reliably distinguished and is
conservatively excluded. New handles/events have priority over idle samples.
The run does not establish actual Z6II speed, AP behavior, secure lock screen
or long-duration OEM background behavior. Physical compatibility still needs
user shooting. Force-stop/process kill/camera hotspot shutdown cannot be
treated as uninterrupted reception. Existing unclassified downloads are not
moved, renamed or assigned invented historical project names.

